Summary:
During today’s session, the focus was on practicing React concepts through simple coding examples. Basic concepts such as components, props, and state were implemented to understand their practical usage. Small examples were created to observe how data flows and how user interactions are handled in React. This hands-on approach helped in reinforcing theoretical understanding with actual coding practice.

Outcomes:
By the end of the session, there was improved confidence in applying React concepts through code. The practice helped in better understanding of component structure and state management. It also strengthened the ability to handle basic user interactions and data flow within applications. Overall, the session enhanced both conceptual clarity and practical coding skills in React.
